"0 0 20 20" width="20" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M5.82275 9.7915C6.19002 9.7915 6.48779 10.0893 6.48779 10.4565V13.4917H9.59619C9.9634 13.4918 10.2612 13.7895 10.2612 14.1567C10.2611 14.5238 9.96332 14.8217 9.59619 14.8218H6.07275C5.56749 14.8218 5.15785 14.412 5.15771 13.9067V10.4565C5.15771 10.0893 5.45548 9.7915 5.82275 9.7915Z" fill="currentColor"></path> <path d="M13.9272 5.17822C14.4324 5.17829 14.8422 5.58807 14.8423 6.09326V9.54346C14.8423 9.91069 14.5445 10.2084 14.1772 10.2085C13.81 10.2085 13.5122 9.91073 13.5122 9.54346V6.5083H10.4038C10.0366 6.50823 9.73877 6.21048 9.73877 5.84326C9.7389 5.47615 10.0367 5.1783 10.4038 5.17822H13.9272Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></button><button type="button" class="no-drag cursor-interaction items-center select-none disabled:cursor-default aria-disabled:cursor-default focus:outline-hidden disabled:opacity-40 aria-disabled:opacity-40 focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-0 whitespace-nowrap flex aspect-square shrink-0 items-center justify-center !px-0 button-p4QQIY controlSurface-VUAmap disabled:text-disabled disabled:opacity-100 aria-disabled:text-disabled aria-disabled:opacity-100" aria-label="Close viewer" data-state="closed"><span class="CompactSource-d7ZD01" aria-hidden="true"><svg aria-hidden="true" class="Icon-X4VkKC" focusable="false" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="16" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><use href="/cdn/assets/icons-aa8c71f949368b4b.svg#codex-icon-xmark-md-light-16" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></span><span class="LeadingSource-d79mNZ" aria-hidden="true"><svg aria-hidden="true" class="Icon-X4VkKC" focusable="false" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="20" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><use href="/cdn/assets/icons-aa8c71f949368b4b.svg#codex-icon-xmark-md-light-20" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></span></button></div></div><div class="pointer-events-auto flex w-max items-center gap-1.5 empty:hidden shrink-0"><div data-menu-overlay-surface="true" class="capsule-uG_Zor controlSurface-VUAmap rounded-full group-lJOwIE empty:hidden inline-flex items-center border-0 text-default shrink-0" aria-label="File actions" role="group"><span class="contents" data-file-tab-action="download"><button type="button" class="no-drag cursor-interaction items-center select-none disabled:cursor-default aria-disabled:cursor-default focus:outline-hidden disabled:opacity-40 aria-disabled:opacity-40 focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-0 whitespace-nowrap flex aspect-square shrink-0 items-center justify-center !px-0 button-p4QQIY controlSurface-VUAmap disabled:text-disabled disabled:opacity-100 aria-disabled:text-disabled aria-disabled:opacity-100" aria-label="Download" aria-busy="false" data-state="closed"><span class="CompactSource-d7ZD01" aria-hidden="true"><svg aria-hidden="true" class="Icon-X4VkKC" focusable="false" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="16" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><use href="/cdn/assets/icons-aa8c71f949368b4b.svg#codex-icon-arrow-down-open-base-light-16" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></span><span class="LeadingSource-d79mNZ" aria-hidden="true"><svg aria-hidden="true" class="Icon-X4VkKC" focusable="false" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="20" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><use href="/cdn/assets/icons-aa8c71f949368b4b.svg#codex-icon-arrow-down-open-base-light-20" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></span></button></span></div></div></div></header><div class="relative min-h-0 flex-1"><div class="relative flex h-full min-h-0 min-w-0 flex-1 overflow-hidden"><div class="flex h-full min-h-0 min-w-0 flex-1 flex-col overflow-hidden"><div class="h-full min-h-0 overflow-y-auto bg-surface text-start"><div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) px-toolbar pt-20 pb-8"><div class="px-4 py-3"><div data-selected-text-overlay-target="_r_7h7_" dir="auto" class="MarkdownRoot-rZKhxa [&amp;&gt;*:first-child]:mt-0 [&amp;&gt;*:last-child]:mb-0 text-size-chat" style="--markdown-link-color: currentColor;"><h1 class="Heading-Ro3lZr" dir="auto">2020KHODA — Local Security Review Addendum</h1><p class="Paragraph-kKnbIo" dir="auto">Date: 2026-11-05<br>Target: <span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">020-d1-candidate.mjs</span><br>Mode: READ-ONLY static review. No source code changed in this review.</p><h2 class="Heading-Ro3lZr" dir="auto">Revalidated checks</h2><ul class="List-kOVW5V UnorderedList-nqKD7g" dir="auto"><li class="ListItem-ncLgmg"><span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">node --check 020-d1-candidate.mjs</span>: PASS</li><li class="ListItem-ncLgmg"><span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">node --check test-020-d1-candidate.mjs</span>: PASS</li><li class="ListItem-ncLgmg"><span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">node test-020-d1-candidate.mjs</span>: 3/3 PASS (mock D1 only)</li></ul><h2 class="Heading-Ro3lZr" dir="auto">Findings</h2><h3 class="Heading-Ro3lZr" dir="auto">S1 — Admin token endpoints have no visible application-level throttling</h3><p class="Paragraph-kKnbIo" dir="auto">The admin gate (<span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">isAdmin</span> / <span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">adminRequired</span>) compares <span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">X-Admin-Token</span> against <span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">env.ADMIN_TOKEN</span>, but the inspected admin handlers do not apply <span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">rateLimit</span> before checking the token. The admin dashboard itself is publicly served, although its data APIs are gated. This does not by itself prove an exploitable weakness: edge-level controls, WAF rules, Access policies, and deployment configuration were not available for review. Nevertheless, an exposed Worker endpoint could permit repeated token guesses unless protected elsewhere.</p><p class="Paragraph-kKnbIo" dir="auto">Recommendation: before release, enforce Cloudflare Access or equivalent edge restriction for admin routes and/or add carefully designed server-side throttling for failed admin authentication. Do not alter auth semantics or token handling until deployment controls are known.</p><h3 class="Heading-Ro3lZr" dir="auto">S2 — Rate limiting depends on <span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">CF-Connecting-IP</span></h3><p class="Paragraph-kKnbIo" dir="auto"><span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">requestIP()</span> falls back to the literal <span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">unknown</span> when the header is absent. In a non-Cloudflare test/proxy environment this can collapse unrelated clients into one bucket; in production Cloudflare normally supplies the header, but that deployment assumption is unverified here.</p><p class="Paragraph-kKnbIo" dir="auto">Recommendation: verify the actual request path and trusted proxy behavior in Staging. Never trust a client-supplied forwarding header as a substitute without a trusted-proxy design.</p><h3 class="Heading-Ro3lZr" dir="auto">S3 — Public lead endpoint is intentionally unauthenticated</h3><p class="Paragraph-kKnbIo" dir="auto"><span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">POST /api/lead</span> accepts public submissions and applies IP rate limiting plus basic name/phone/email validation. This is consistent with public lead capture, but the reviewed code does not show CAPTCHA, honeypot, or abuse scoring. Spam resistance is therefore not established.</p><p class="Paragraph-kKnbIo" dir="auto">Recommendation: consider an abuse-control layer after verifying business requirements; do not block legitimate lead conversion flows.</p><h3 class="Heading-Ro3lZr" dir="auto">S4 — Origin validation is applied to auth routes, not uniformly</h3><p class="Paragraph-kKnbIo" dir="auto"><span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">isAllowedOrigin()</span> is called in <span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">handleAuth</span>. Other cookie-authenticated routes rely in part on <span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">SameSite=Strict</span>; the public guest cookie uses <span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">SameSite=Lax</span>. No CORS <span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">Access-Control-Allow-Origin</span> is emitted by the inspected OPTIONS handler. A complete CSRF assessment requires endpoint-by-endpoint request semantics and deployed domain configuration.</p><p class="Paragraph-kKnbIo" dir="auto">Recommendation: perform CSRF testing in Staging before release. Do not assume the helper protects routes where it is not called.</p><h2 class="Heading-Ro3lZr" dir="auto">Positive observations (limited to inspected code)</h2><ul class="List-kOVW5V UnorderedList-nqKD7g" dir="auto"><li class="ListItem-ncLgmg">Session cookies are marked <span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">HttpOnly</span>, <span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">Secure</span>, and <span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">SameSite=Strict</span>.</li><li class="ListItem-ncLgmg">Session tokens are generated from cryptographically secure random bytes; only a SHA-256 token hash is stored.</li><li class="ListItem-ncLgmg">Password derivation uses PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA-256 with 100,000 iterations and per-user random salt in the current registration path.</li><li class="ListItem-ncLgmg">SQL values in inspected D1 helpers are bound with prepared statements. Dynamic settings column names are selected from a fixed allowlist derived from <span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">PRAGMA table_info</span>.</li><li class="ListItem-ncLgmg">CRM dashboard rendering of lead fields uses <span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">textContent</span>, not HTML interpolation. The inspected <span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">innerHTML</span> uses are static UI fragments or clearing containers.</li><li class="ListItem-ncLgmg">Chat ownership is checked before reading/updating an authenticated user's chat.</li></ul><h2 class="Heading-Ro3lZr" dir="auto">Not verified</h2><ul class="List-kOVW5V UnorderedList-nqKD7g" dir="auto"><li class="ListItem-ncLgmg">Actual D1 schema, constraints, indexes, migrations, and production data compatibility.</li><li class="ListItem-ncLgmg">Cloudflare Access/WAF/rate-limiting configuration, environment bindings, secrets, routes, domains, or Worker runtime behavior.</li><li class="ListItem-ncLgmg">End-to-end authentication, password compatibility with existing users, session expiry/revocation, admin access, CSRF, abuse resistance, and multi-user isolation against a real database.</li><li class="ListItem-ncLgmg">Full security audit or penetration test.</li></ul><h2 class="Heading-Ro3lZr" dir="auto">Release decision</h2><p class="Paragraph-kKnbIo" dir="auto"><strong class="font-semibold">NO-GO remains unchanged.</strong> This addendum identifies review items; it does not authorize code changes or deployment. Original source and Candidate remain unchanged by this addendum.</p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-y-0 end-0 grid min-h-0 max-w-full min-w-0 pt-13"></div></div></div></section></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></aside></div></main></div><div id="DndDescribedBy-24" style="display: none;">
    To pick up a draggable item, press the space bar.
