up-data-[print-formatting]/conversation-print:items-start items-end"><div data-user-message-bubble="true" class="bg-user-message text-user-message min-w-0 max-w-(--user-chat-width) overflow-hidden break-words px-(--thread-content-margin) [&amp;_.contain-inline-size]:[contain:initial] bubble-vBnidZ py-2.5 rounded-2xl relative text-start"><div class="flex flex-col items-end gap-1"><div class="relative w-full min-w-0 text-size-chat leading-relaxed"><div class=""><div><div class="text-size-chat whitespace-pre-wrap"><div data-selected-text-overlay-target="_r_7ku_" dir="auto" data-markdown-text-tone="user-message" class="MarkdownRoot-rZKhxa [&amp;&gt;*:first-child]:mt-0 [&amp;&gt;*:last-child]:mb-0 [&amp;_ol]:!ps-6 [&amp;_ul]:!ps-6 rich-text-user-turn" style="--markdown-link-color: currentColor;"><h1 class="Heading-Ro3lZr" dir="auto"><span>2020KHODA — Local Security Review Addendum</span></h1><p class="Paragraph-kKnbIo" dir="auto"><span>Date: 2026-11-05</span><br><span>Target: </span><span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">020-d1-candidate.mjs</span><br><span>Mode: READ-ONLY static review. No source code changed in this review.</span></p><h2 class="Heading-Ro3lZr" dir="auto"><span>Revalidated checks</span></h2><ul class="List-kOVW5V UnorderedList-nqKD7g" dir="auto"><li class="ListItem-ncLgmg"><span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">node --check 020-d1-candidate.mjs</span><span>: PASS</span></li><li class="ListItem-ncLgmg"><span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">node --check test-020-d1-candidate.mjs</span><span>: PASS</span></li><li class="ListItem-ncLgmg"><span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">node test-020-d1-candidate.mjs</span><span>: 3/3 PASS (mock D1 only)</span></li></ul><h2 class="Heading-Ro3lZr" dir="auto"><span>Findings</span></h2><h3 class="Heading-Ro3lZr" dir="auto"><span>S1 — Admin token endpoints have no visible application-level throttling</span></h3><p class="Paragraph-kKnbIo" dir="auto"><span>The admin gate (</span><span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">isAdmin</span><span> / </span><span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">adminRequired</span><span>) compares </span><span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">X-Admin-Token</span><span> against </span><span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">env.ADMIN_TOKEN</span><span>, but the inspected admin handlers do not apply </span><span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">rateLimit</span><span> before checking the token. The admin dashboard itself is publicly served, although its data APIs are gated. This does not by itself prove an exploitable weakness: edge-level controls, WAF rules, Access policies, and deployment configuration were not available for review. Nevertheless, an exposed Worker endpoint could permit repeated token guesses unless protected elsewhere.</span></p><p class="Paragraph-kKnbIo" dir="auto"><span>Recommendation: before release, enforce Cloudflare Access or equivalent edge restriction for admin routes and/or add carefully designed server-side throttling for failed admin authentication. Do not alter auth semantics or token handling until deployment controls are known.</span></p><h3 class="Heading-Ro3lZr" dir="auto"><span>S2 — Rate limiting depends on </span><span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">CF-Connecting-IP</span></h3><p class="Paragraph-kKnbIo" dir="auto"><span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">requestIP()</span><span> falls back to the literal </span><span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">unknown</span><span> when the header is absent. In a non-Cloudflare test/proxy environment this can collapse unrelated clients into one bucket; in production Cloudflare normally supplies the header, but that deployment assumption is unverified here.</span></p><p class="Paragraph-kKnbIo" dir="auto"><span>Recommendation: verify the actual request path and trusted proxy behavior in Staging. Never trust a client-supplied forwarding header as a substitute without a trusted-proxy design.</span></p><h3 class="Heading-Ro3lZr" dir="auto"><span>S3 — Public lead endpoint is intentionally unauthenticated</span></h3><p class="Paragraph-kKnbIo" dir="auto"><span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">POST /api/lead</span><span> accepts public submissions and applies IP rate limiting plus basic name/phone/email validation. This is consistent with public lead capture, but the reviewed code does not show CAPTCHA, honeypot, or abuse scoring. Spam resistance is therefore not established.</span></p><p class="Paragraph-kKnbIo" dir="auto"><span>Recommendation: consider an abuse-control layer after verifying business requirements; do not block legitimate lead conversion flows.</span></p><h3 class="Heading-Ro3lZr" dir="auto"><span>S4 — Origin validation is applied to auth routes, not uniformly</span></h3><p class="Paragraph-kKnbIo" dir="auto"><span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">isAllowedOrigin()</span><span> is called in </span><span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">handleAuth</span><span>. Other cookie-authenticated routes rely in part on </span><span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">SameSite=Strict</span><span>; the public guest cookie uses </span><span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">SameSite=Lax</span><span>. No CORS </span><span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">Access-Control-Allow-Origin</span><span> is emitted by the inspected OPTIONS handler. A complete CSRF assessment requires endpoint-by-endpoint request semantics and deployed domain configuration.</span></p><p class="Paragraph-kKnbIo" dir="auto"><span>Recommendation: perform CSRF testing in Staging before release. Do not assume the helper protects routes where it is not called.</span></p><h2 class="Heading-Ro3lZr" dir="auto"><span>Positive observations (limited to inspected code)</span></h2><ul class="List-kOVW5V UnorderedList-nqKD7g" dir="auto"><li class="ListItem-ncLgmg"><span>Session cookies are marked </span><span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">HttpOnly</span><span>, </span><span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">Secure</span><span>, and </span><span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">SameSite=Strict</span><span>.</span></li><li class="ListItem-ncLgmg"><span>Session tokens are generated from cryptographically secure random bytes; only a SHA-256 token hash is stored.</span></li><li class="ListItem-ncLgmg"><span>Password derivation uses PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA-256 with 100,000 iterations and per-user random salt in the current registration path.</span></li><li class="ListItem-ncLgmg"><span>SQL values in inspected D1 helpers are bound with prepared statements. Dynamic settings column names are selected from a fixed allowlist derived from </span><span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">PRAGMA table_info</span><span>.</span></li><li class="ListItem-ncLgmg"><span>CRM dashboard rendering of lead fields uses </span><span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">textContent</span><span>, not HTML interpolation. The inspected </span><span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">innerHTML</span><span> uses are static UI fragments or clearing containers.</span></li><li class="ListItem-ncLgmg"><span>Chat ownership is checked before reading/updating an authenticated user's chat.</span></li></ul><h2 class="Heading-Ro3lZr" dir="auto"><span>Not verified</span></h2><ul class="List-kOVW5V UnorderedList-nqKD7g" dir="auto"><li class="ListItem-ncLgmg"><span>Actual D1 schema, constraints, indexes, migrations, and production data compatibility.</span></li><li class="ListItem-ncLgmg"><span>Cloudflare Access/WAF/rate-limiting configuration, environment bindings, secrets, routes, domains, or Worker runtime behavior.</span></li><li class="ListItem-ncLgmg"><span>End-to-end authentication, password compatibility with existing users, session expiry/revocation, admin access, CSRF, abuse resistance, and multi-user isolation against a real database.</span></li><li class="ListItem-ncLgmg"><span>Full security audit or penetration test.</span></li></ul><h2 class="Heading-Ro3lZr" dir="auto"><span>Release decision</span></h2><p class="Paragraph-kKnbIo" dir="auto"><strong class="font-semibold"><span>NO-GO remains unchanged.</span></strong><span> This addendum identifies review items; it does not authorize code changes or deployment. Original source and Candidate remain unchanged by this addendum.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="flex flex-row-reverse items-center gap-1"><div class="isolate me-1 ms-1 flex items-center gap-2 opacity-0 group-has-[:focus-visible]/user-message:opacity-100 group-hover/user-message:opacity-100 [@media(